<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incĭno</span></b> , ĕre,
			v. a. and n.
		in-cano, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to blow</i> or <i>sound</i>, <i>to sing</i> (very rare; not in Cic.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">varios incinit ore modos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					2, 22</span></i>
			 (3, 15), 6: frequentamenta quaedam varia, <i><span class="en">Gell. 1,
				11, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si modulislenibus tibicen incinat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					4, 13, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
